{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/lib/feedback-config.py","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:44:36.357187Z","id":"e9c6a9d28c8dd3f5f74eb70702534a5027842b94bcde954604d71de7bd80da3f","body":{"detail":"write writes <config>.tmp.<pid> and os.replace()s it over the config; an error between open and replace (disk full, chmod failing) leaves the temp file. It holds no secret (the grant is in its own file), only the config text.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"c2c3b65b970d29ea2776aef3c9d35580a1489274f2b44cbd2d222a982f11ed18"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap the write in try/finally that removes the temp file unless it was replaced.","summary":"feedback-config.py leaves its temp file behind when a write fails","tags":["feedback","scripts","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/lib/release-common.sh","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:56:47.896324Z","id":"a547e0106da18241c972d4752813467242b6de5954db95a93923f5f18afde498","body":{"detail":"release-sdk.sh's publish step is judged done by has_version (`npm view PKG@V version`, scripts/lib/release-common.sh:105), which reads npm's cached packument and can lag a publish by minutes. publish_through (lines 240-261) treats a 'completed success' run like a failed one ('a success leaves the version on npm, which the caller checks first') and dispatches anew. A rerun of `just release-sdk` shortly after a run that stopped while waiting (await_run giving up after repeated gh failures, or the terminal closed) can therefore dispatch a second run that builds for minutes, then fails 'already on npm' or at npm publish, and the script then suggests `gh run rerun --failed` (line 212), which fails the same way.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":261}},"suggested_fix":"In publish_through, return 0 when the found run is 'completed success' (the caller already knows npm lacked the version, so it can then await_output npm_version as the first publish does), and dispatch anew only for a failed or cancelled run.","summary":"publish_through dispatches a new publish run when it finds a successful one, which happens whenever npm's registry view has not caught up with that success","tags":["review","review:pr45-client-split","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"scripts/lib/release-common.sh","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:42:08.572351Z","id":"11c7fdedb1de666896951344c77980322b86686818a28152dd5abd39230bb816","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4c5d96d3d","summary":"publish_through (scripts/lib/release-common.sh) returns 0 for a run found 'completed success' instead of dispatching; release-sdk.sh's step_4 (and release.sh's step_20) then await_output npm's listing of the version. test-release-sdk.sh case_12 'a publish run that succeeded is waited on through npm, not dispatched again' passes (bash scripts/test-release-sdk.sh: 30 PASS, 0 FAIL; it fails against the previous scripts).","supersedes":"a547e0106da18241c972d4752813467242b6de5954db95a93923f5f18afde498","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
